.TH PSDiagonalFlattenVector 3 2023-12-07 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSDiagonalFlattenVector

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSMatrix  
.br
\fBPSDiagonalFlattenVector\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a matrix of shape \fIlen\fR, \fIlen\fR where values of vector \fIvec\fR having length defined by \fIlen\fR are distributed over a diagonal line starting from top-left side and ending to bottom-right side.
.br
Example:
.br


PSFLoat vec[4] = {1, 2, 3, 4};
.br
PSDiagonalFlattenVector(vec, 4); // ->
.br
// {1, 0, 0, 0,
.br
//  0, 2, 0, 0,
.br
//  0, 0, 3, 0,
.br
//  0, 0, 0 ,4}
.br




.SH RETURN VALUES
The matrix or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIvec\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIlen\fR is zero.
.br

\[bu] The matrix cannot be allocated in memory.
.br
.RE
